<title>BRAZIL: BRAZIL REALTY H1 NET INCOME SLIPS.</title>
<headline>BRAZIL REALTY H1 NET INCOME SLIPS.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian-Argentine real estate company Brazil Realty on Tuesday issued the following statement on its first half results.</p>
<p>			   H1 1997		  H1 1996</p>
<p>    Net income	 2.97 million	   6.45 million</p>
<p>    Net sales	 10.61 million	   2.62 million</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures in Brazilian reais.</p>
<p>Brazil Realty is a joint venture between Brazilian real estate developer Elie Horn and IRSA - Inversiones y Representaciones Sociedad Anonima, an Argentine real estate company that is partially controlled by investor George Soros, the company said in a statement.</p>
</text>
